<title>USA: US exporters report soybean oil sold to China-USDA.</title>
<headline>US exporters report soybean oil sold to China-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Monday private exporters reported sales of 22,000 tonnes of soybean oil to China for delivery during the 1996/97 marketing year.</p>
<p>The marketing year for soybean oil began Oct 1.</p>
<p>Exporters must report to USDA sales of 20,000 tonnes or more of soybean oil made in one day to a single destination by 1500 ET the next business day after the sale.</p>
<p>Sales of lesser quantities must be reported weekly.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8394))</p>
</text>
